            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A multi-tenant, cloud-hosted Network Access Control (NAC) system may receive an indicator from a Network Access Server (NAS) device to identify the tenant with which the NAS device is associated. The NAS device may put the identifier in the Transport Layer Security (TLS)/ Secure Sockets Layer (SSL) extension Server Name Indication (SNI) field. The NAC system may use the identifier to obtain tenant-specific configuration information for setting up a secure tunnel with the NAS device.</p>
            </abstract>
